{{smaller block|The king proposed nothing more than to ''unite'' his kingdom in one form of worship. {{right|''Clarendon'', Great Rebellion.}}}}

'''4.''' To cause to adhere; attach; connect together: as, to ''unite'' bricks or stones by means of cement.
{{smaller block|The peritonæum, which is a dry body, may be ''united'' with the musculous flesh. {{right|''Wiseman'', Surgery.}}}}
